# Comments must be on their own line: git treats a `#` after a pattern as part
# of the pattern, silently disabling it.

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target
/dist
**/*.rs.bk
# coverage instrumentation
*.profraw
# MSVC debug symbols beside a Windows build
*.pdb

# ── What hiewLM itself writes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The tool leaves files *next to the sample it is looking at*. Anyone who runs it
# on a file inside a checkout would otherwise commit their analysis by accident —
# and analysis of a sample can be sensitive.
#
# atomic save keeps one, as <name>.<ext>.bak
*.bak
# the temporary file an atomic save renames into place
*.hiewlm.tmp
# legacy colour-marker sidecar (still read, for migration)
*.hiewlm.markers
# `Y` then `w` writes <sample>.triage.md
*.triage.md
# resources extracted from a PE with Enter in the header view
res_*.bin

# Notes are keyed by content hash and live in the user's data directory, not
# beside the sample, so there is nothing to ignore for those.

# ── Samples ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository holds no malware, and must not start holding any by accident.
*.exe
*.dll
*.sys
*.scr
*.msi
# …except the harmless test binaries in assets/samples, which are deliberate.
!assets/samples/**

# ── Editors and IDEs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── Operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Never ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
*.pem
*.key
secrets.toml

# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#   Cargo.lock       a workspace that ships binaries pins its dependencies
#   assets/samples/  small, harmless programs for exercising the parsers by hand
